> Lichen and lizard corpses do not rot, and can be carried around for
> emergency food. Lizard corpses also have the extremely useful effect
> of curing delayed-stoning attacks by cockatrices and chickatrices
> ("You are slowing down", "Your limbs are stiffening"); lizards start
> showing up about the time cockatrices and chickatrices do, so when you
> see a lizard kill it, keep your pet from eating it and save that
> corpse!

Lichens have a completely different advantage that culd be spoiled
separately.

The third one related to this category is acid blob corpses.  They do
rot away in the usual range of time, but they never give food poison. 
While in the mines where there is a chance of polymorph traps and
before lizards start to appear it's a good idea to kill acid blobs
(throwing rocks so you don't damage your items) and carry the corpse
just in case you enounter a monster with a stoning attack.  The chances
of enountering such a monster is low but the cost of the carry is also
low.  Once I have a lizard in my inventory I ignore acid blobs, but by
then i'm usually deep enough that few are generated any more.


